  "note": "Round 19 r19-helperfn (TwHelperFn, rebased from round-18 drafts/tripwire/r18-helperfn). Two rules. (A) A function defined earlier in the SAME command text and called there with literal arguments has its body classified with those arguments substituted ($1..$9/$@/$* for shell functions, positional parameters for python `def`); positives show the resolved command, negatives show that nothing is guessed (uncalled, non-literal, wrong order, redefined, vararg, non-spawn body, non-literal default, single-quoted $1, call before definition). (B) A call to a name the text neither defines nor imports, handed a literal positional ['prog', ...] argv list that classifies as a host command, is reported as a lead (the real r13-root.jsonl:4 shape); pure data calls and calls to same-text defs with non-literal arguments contribute nothing. Two round-18 pins changed with the round-18 `pacman` fail-safe (unknown operator -> host_mutation): sh-fn-positional-n and sh-fn-single-quoted.",
